# No key is needed. Both keys below are an OPTIONAL upgrade (better POI data, live opening
# hours, real transit routes, full Google map in the viewer).
# Without a key: `places` uses OpenStreetMap Nominatim (data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors,
# throttled to 1 request/second), `routes`/`optimize` use straight-line estimates, and the
# viewer draws its map on darkened OpenStreetMap tiles, with a keyless "Google 預覽" mode.
# Google Maps Platform key (Places API (New), Routes API, Maps JavaScript API).
# Used by the CLI (GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY) and the viewer (VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY).
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# VITE_ keys are bundled into the web page: use a separate key, Maps JavaScript API only,
# restricted to HTTP referrer http://localhost:*/* .
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Basemap under the viewer's interactive map: osm (default, OpenStreetMap tiles darkened in the
# browser; light personal use only, attribution shown), none (fully offline grid), or an https URL
# template with {z} {x} {y} (and optionally {s}, {r}) for another tile provider you are allowed to use.
VITE_MAP_TILES=

# Optional: sync a trip to Notion so you can read it on your phone (`npm run tripcode -- export notion <tripId>`).
# One-time setup:
#   1. https://www.notion.so/profile/integrations -> New integration (Internal) -> copy the secret.
#   2. In Notion, open the page that should hold your trips -> ... -> Connections -> add your integration.
#   3. Copy that page's URL (or the 32-character id at its end).
NOTION_TOKEN=
NOTION_PARENT_PAGE_ID=
